  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e2effc6c8484a4541877dbfe23a82f8a, type: 3}
  m_Name: Story4NPC1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  sentences:
  - name: Mother
    text: I told him not to trust uniforms. Not his. Theirs. He laughed at me. Said
      I worried too much and that things are different now.
  - name: Mother
    text: "I have lived long enough to know that \u2018different\u2019 is just another
      way of saying \u2018not for everyone.\u2019"
  - name: Mother
    text: "People from home would laugh like it was a joke. \u2018A cop?\u2019 they\u2019d
      say. \u2018With your face?\u2019  Like it was a costume he had no right to
      wear. "
  - name: Mother
    text: Jokes are how people tell the truth without taking responsibility. He wanted
      to prove them wrong. Wanted to show that you can serve a place without erasing
      where you come from.
  - name: Mother
    text: "I go to church more often now. It gives me words when I don\u2019t have
      my own. God sees effort.  He didn\u2019t need that."
  - name: Mother
    text: "He believed in action. In being \u2018a good man.\u2019 Now I pray differently.
      Not for answers. Just that his name is said correctly. That he is not reduced
      to an error."
  - name: Mother
    text: " Maybe that\u2019s why this hurts so much. He did everything they say
      they want from a good man.  And still, they didn\u2019t recognize him."
  - name: Mother
    text: "I\u2019ll light a candle. It\u2019s something I can still do for my son.
      Even now."
